-- | Placeholder module for the `pds/` project skeleton (S-pds-skeleton).
--
-- Its ONLY job is to prove the `pds/test/*.mdk` -> `pds/lib/*.mdk` import
-- wiring works before any real module depends on it. The first slice that
-- lands a real `pds/lib/` module may delete this file.
--
-- 🚨 SKELETON DELETION PROTOCOL [RUN-PDS0-003(c)] — a THREE-PART COUPLED
-- EDIT, ALL-OR-NOTHING, in one commit, if this file is ever deleted:
--   (1) delete pds/lib/skeleton.mdk;
--   (2) drop its import from pds/test/skeleton_test.mdk;
--   (3) lower the SUITES floor in pds/test/inlang_test_oracle.sh to the
--       assertion count that actually remains.
-- Doing part of it either reds the gate (import of a deleted module) or —
-- worse — silently lowers the anti-rot floor. pds/test/skeleton_test.mdk and
-- the gate script itself are NEVER deleted.

export skeletonOk : Bool
skeletonOk = True
